# interplay_memlive_alias_writeback_race: Two tasks' private buffers over one guest page, each filling a different half with invalidateGuest and synchronize (6): task 1 its first 0x20 bytes, then task 2 (paged from the page after task 1's write-back, invalidateHost) bytes 0x20-0x3f, then task 1 bytes 0x40-0x5f with flags 6 again. In-process a synchronize copies the whole host copy back over the page, so each write-back erases what the other task wrote since its copy was paged: the page ends with task 1's host copy, and task 2's bytes are lost. In the service both buffers are the page itself, and every fill survives.
